{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\n\n\nstruct DSU\n{\n\tvector<ll> parent;\n\n\tDSU(ll n)\n\t{\n\t\tparent = vector<ll>(n);\n\t\tfor (ll i = 0LL; i < n; i++) {\n\t\t\tparent[i] = i;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tll find_set(ll a)\n\t{\n\t\tif (a == parent[a]) {\n\t\t\treturn a;\n\t\t}\n\t\tll base = find_set(parent[a]);\n\t\tparent[a] = base;\n\t\treturn base;\n\t}\n\n\tvoid union_set(ll a, ll b)\n\t{\n\t\ta = find_set(a);\n\t\tb = find_set(b);\n\t\tif (a != b) {\n\t\t\tif (rand() % 2) {\n\t\t\t\tswap(a, b);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tparent[b] = a;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n};\n\nll count_cycles(ll p, ll k)\n{\n\tDSU dsu(p);\n\tfor (ll i = 1LL; i < p; i++) {\n\t\tll ki = (k * i) % p;\n\t\tdsu.union_set(i, ki);\n\t}\n\n\tvector<bool> found(p, false);\n\tll count = 0LL;\n\tfor (ll i = 1LL; i < p; i++) {\n\t\tll base = dsu.find_set(i);\n\t\tif (!found[base]) {\n\t\t\tfound[base] = true;\n\t\t\tcount++;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn count;\n}\n\nll count_solutions(ll p, ll k)\n{\n\tll cycles;\n\tif (k == 0) {\n\t\tcycles = p - 1;\n\t}\n\telse if (k == 1) {\n\t\tcycles = p;\n\t}\n\telse {\n\t\tcycles = count_cycles(p, k);\n\t}\n\n\tll count = 1LL;\n\tfor (ll i = 0LL; i < cycles; i++) {\n\t\tcount *= (ll)p;\n\t\tcount %= MOD;\n\t}\n\treturn (ll)count;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n\tll p, k;\n\tcin >> p >> k;\n\tll count = count_solutions(p, k);\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\", count);\n\n\tint end;\n\tcin >> end;\n\treturn 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport random\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\nclass DSU:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.parent = list(range(n))\n\n    def find_set(self, a):\n        if a == self.parent[a]:\n            return a\n        base = self.find_set(self.parent[a])\n        self.parent[a] = base\n        return base\n\n    def union_set(self, a, b):\n        a = self.find_set(a)\n        b = self.find_set(b)\n        if a != b:\n            if random.randint(0, 1):\n                a, b = b, a\n            self.parent[b] = a\n\ndef count_cycles(p, k):\n    dsu = DSU(p)\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        ki = (k * i) % p\n        dsu.union_set(i, ki)\n    found = [False] * p\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        base = dsu.find_set(i)\n        if not found[base]:\n            found[base] = True\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef count_solutions(p, k):\n    if k == 0:\n        cycles = p - 1\n    elif k == 1:\n        cycles = p\n    else:\n        cycles = count_cycles(p, k)\n    count = 1\n    for _ in range(cycles):\n        count *= p\n        count %= MOD\n    return count\n\ndef main():\n    p, k = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    result = count_solutions(p, k)\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.4836123e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.000558101